      "instance_name": "pun_on_nose",
      "label": "Pun on 'nose' as a play on 'know'",
      "description": "The meme uses a linguistic pun by replacing 'know' with 'nose' in the phrase 'I know it will be good' to reference Voldemort's long, pointed nose. This pun is a form of wordplay that requires knowledge of the character's physical appearance and the original line to be understood. It is a common technique in internet memes to create humor through wordplay and visual juxtaposition.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_32f2b9f6"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
